#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-key-generate-secret.md:36
msgid "Description"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-key-generate-secret.md:38
msgid ""
"This command generates a new Ed25519 secret key for signing store paths and "
"prints it on standard output. Use `nix key convert-secret-to-public` to get "
"the corresponding public key for verifying signed store paths."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-key-generate-secret.md:43
msgid ""
"The mandatory argument `--key-name` specifies a key name (such as `cache."
"example.org-1`). It is used to look up keys on the client when it verifies "
"signatures. It can be anything, but it’s suggested to use the host name of "
"your cache (e.g.  `cache.example.org`) with a suffix denoting the number of "
"the key (to be incremented every time you need to revoke a key)."
msgstr ""

